    <string name="explain_mixes">Ready-made mixes as a starting point. Then adjust any slider as you like.</string>
    <string name="explain_colors">Each colour has its own slider, mix them freely. All are set equally loud, they differ only in sound. Grey and green are approximations.</string>
    <string name="explain_white">bright and hissing, all frequencies equally strong</string>
    <string name="explain_pink">balanced, like rain; softer highs than white</string>
    <string name="explain_brown">deep, like surf; even fewer highs</string>
    <string name="explain_grey">roughly evens out how the ear hears highs and lows, so it sounds equally loud everywhere</string>
    <string name="explain_green">brings out the middle around 500 Hz, soft and natural</string>
    <string name="explain_waves">The wave button next to a colour makes it swell and fade like ocean waves: rising, breaking, running out, each wave a little different. Below it you set how long the waves are on average (3 to 20 s). While playing, the slider moves along.</string>
    <string name="explain_volume">Quiet is enough: noises should blur, it need not be louder than a calm conversation. For children, a speaker is better than headphones. Treble: left sounds duller, right brighter.</string>
    <string name="explain_timer">The timer fades out gently at the end instead of stopping hard, over up to 2 minutes for long timers. If you change it while playing, it starts over.</string>
